            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allergic rhinitis is the most common form of allergy with a prevalence of 30%. Allergic rhinitis is associated with substantial health economic costs and patient suffering. Asthma is strongly associated with allergic rhinitis. The treatment of allergic rhinitis should be individualized and include the whole airway. The treatment goals should be a patient free of symptoms affecting their daily life or sleep.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
